
# Access Control

  1. private 

      Only accessible inside the class and inside the extension, but if the extension is on another file and a private variable is on another file then you won't be able to access.
  

      private(set) var balance = 20  (Now you can only get or read from outside)

  2. fileprivate

      Within the file you can access it in the class or in the extension, but outside the file you won't be able to access.

  3. interval

      If you don't put anytpe, be default is internal, and can be access anywhere in the targets
    
  4. public

      You can access it in any tagets, if you want to expose it outside of frameworks you can mark it as public, you won't be allowed to extend or inherit
  
  5. open

      You can access it in any tagets, if you want to expose it outside of frameworks you can mark it  open, it alow you to extend and inherit

  6. package


  class Account{
    var balance: Double = 20
  }

  extension Account{
    
  }
  
  let account: Account()
print(account.balance)


# Higher Order Functions


Take another function or parameter or parameter and return a function or closure


1- map

  let number = [1,2,3,4,5]

  let result = number.map {number in 
  return number * 2 
  }

2. compactmap

    It is same as map, but if it have the nil and optional, it will remove all of them 

    let number = ["1","2","3","4","5","abc"]
    let result = number.compactMap { Int($0) }
    print(result)

3. reduce

    Main use is if you have a collectiona and you want to reduce it to single element, then you apply reduce mostly addition or multiplication, or fibbnoci series
  
4. flatMap

    If you have two dimensional array, it will convert it to one dimensional array

      let twoDimArray = [[1,2], [3,4], [5,6], [7,8]]
      print(twoDimArray.flatMap($0))
  
5. filter

    To apply filter operations  like you have an array and you want to filter out the even numbers, it will filter


  let number = [1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9]

  let evenNumber = number.filter { $0 % 2 == 0 }
  print(evenNumber)

6. sort

  sorted() ->  it will return you a new array of sorting elements, original array will remain same.

  sort() ->    It will not return you anything, it will modified or sort the original array , not give you any new array

7. foreach

  Similar like For loop , insted of putting for loop, we use forEach closure

  number.forEach {
    print($0)
  }













